WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.033 --> 00:00:00.200
A new

00:00:00.200 --> 00:00:01.334
report released by

00:00:01.334 --> 00:00:03.370
special counsel John Durham concludes

00:00:03.370 --> 00:00:05.238
the FBI should never have launched

00:00:05.238 --> 00:00:06.139
its 2016

00:00:06.139 --> 00:00:07.907
Russia investigation in the first place.

00:00:07.907 --> 00:00:09.709
Durham, who was picked by the Trump

00:00:09.709 --> 00:00:10.910
administration, writes

00:00:10.910 --> 00:00:13.780
that the over 300 page report details

00:00:13.780 --> 00:00:14.714
a four year probe

00:00:14.714 --> 00:00:15.482
which yielded

00:00:15.482 --> 00:00:17.684
very little in terms of prosecutions.

00:00:17.717 --> 00:00:18.818
He adds, quote,

00:00:18.818 --> 00:00:20.987
The FBI used raw and analyzed

00:00:20.987 --> 00:00:23.023
and uncorroborated intelligence

00:00:23.023 --> 00:00:25.091
and, quote, ignored material information

00:00:25.091 --> 00:00:26.860
that did not support the narrative

00:00:26.860 --> 00:00:28.194
of a collusive relationship

00:00:28.194 --> 00:00:29.863
between Trump and Russia.

00:00:29.863 --> 00:00:30.530
We should note

00:00:30.530 --> 00:00:31.831
this report is at odds

00:00:31.831 --> 00:00:33.233
with the 2019

00:00:33.233 --> 00:00:35.502
DOJ inspector general's findings

00:00:35.502 --> 00:00:36.636
that there was a basis,

00:00:36.636 --> 00:00:37.704
a legitimate reason

00:00:37.704 --> 00:00:39.639
to open this investigation

00:00:39.639 --> 00:00:40.473
So let's talk about it

00:00:40.473 --> 00:00:41.741
with CNN senior law enforcement

00:00:41.741 --> 00:00:42.976
analyst Andy McCabe.

00:00:42.976 --> 00:00:43.943
He's the former deputy

00:00:43.943 --> 00:00:45.378
director of the FBI.

00:00:45.378 --> 00:00:47.313
And importantly, he oversaw

00:00:47.313 --> 00:00:48.214
what became known

00:00:48.214 --> 00:00:49.082
as a CROSSFIRE

00:00:49.082 --> 00:00:51.785
hurricane probe into Trump in 2016.

00:00:51.785 --> 00:00:53.987
And Andy your name is in this report

00:00:53.987 --> 00:00:56.222
almost 60 times 58 times the morning.

00:00:57.824 --> 00:00:58.892
Morning in your

00:00:58.892 --> 00:00:59.359
words you

00:00:59.359 --> 00:01:00.226
were quote deeply

00:01:00.226 --> 00:01:01.394
involved in the decision

00:01:01.394 --> 00:01:02.595
to open the investigation

00:01:02.595 --> 00:01:04.130
John Durham

00:01:04.130 --> 00:01:06.099
says that you shouldn't have launched it.

00:01:06.099 --> 00:01:07.734
What's your response

00:01:08.635 --> 00:01:10.070
John Durham is wrong

00:01:10.070 --> 00:01:11.371
and it's not just me

00:01:11.371 --> 00:01:13.339
that says that every other entity

00:01:13.339 --> 00:01:15.341
that's investigated

00:01:15.341 --> 00:01:18.545
our in our activities in 2016 agrees

00:01:18.678 --> 00:01:21.181
and that's of course as you mentioned

00:01:21.181 --> 00:01:22.582
the DOJ

00:01:22.582 --> 00:01:23.349
inspector general

00:01:23.349 --> 00:01:24.717
Michael Horowitz

00:01:24.717 --> 00:01:25.685
as well as the Senate

00:01:25.685 --> 00:01:27.120
Intelligence Committee led

00:01:27.120 --> 00:01:29.422
of course at the time by a Republican.

00:01:31.391 --> 00:01:33.793
So this is this

00:01:33.793 --> 00:01:36.362
report Poppy stands as an anomaly.

00:01:37.030 --> 00:01:37.931
I have my own theories

00:01:37.931 --> 00:01:39.799
as to why it stands as an anomaly.

00:01:39.799 --> 00:01:41.101
I don't think this investigation

00:01:41.101 --> 00:01:42.936
was legitimate from its inception.

00:01:42.936 --> 00:01:43.403
Why?

00:01:45.171 --> 00:01:47.340
Because simply because John Durham

00:01:47.340 --> 00:01:48.108
made clear

00:01:48.108 --> 00:01:49.109
from the very beginning,

00:01:49.109 --> 00:01:50.543
shortly after he was appointed

00:01:50.543 --> 00:01:52.212
exactly what he was going to conclude.

00:01:52.212 --> 00:01:53.513
He's made public remarks

00:01:53.513 --> 00:01:55.982
indicating that he thought that we had

00:01:55.982 --> 00:01:56.916
possibly broken

00:01:56.916 --> 00:01:59.152
the law and inappropriately investigated

00:01:59.152 --> 00:01:59.586
the president,

00:01:59.586 --> 00:02:01.888
which is an odd thing for any

00:02:01.888 --> 00:02:03.590
then US attorney to do

00:02:03.590 --> 00:02:05.225
at the beginning of an investigation.

00:02:05.225 --> 00:02:07.627
I echoed the same sentiments of

00:02:07.627 --> 00:02:08.328
of his boss

00:02:08.328 --> 00:02:08.962
William Barr,

00:02:08.962 --> 00:02:10.296
who was attorney general at the time.

00:02:10.296 --> 00:02:12.232
So I don't think it's surprising

00:02:12.232 --> 00:02:13.900
where the where the report came out.

00:02:13.900 --> 00:02:15.635
It's disappointing.

00:02:15.635 --> 00:02:17.303
And it continues to fuel a false

00:02:17.303 --> 00:02:18.638
narrative about

00:02:18.638 --> 00:02:19.706
alleged FBI

00:02:19.706 --> 00:02:21.708
malfeasance that continues to this day,

00:02:21.708 --> 00:02:23.910
almost seven years after the events

00:02:24.210 --> 00:02:24.944
in question.

00:02:26.012 --> 00:02:27.013
But, you know,

00:02:27.013 --> 00:02:28.381
as I said, I'm not surprised.

00:02:28.381 --> 00:02:28.781
I'll note

00:02:28.781 --> 00:02:30.884
at the time that he was appointed by Bill

00:02:30.884 --> 00:02:31.117
Barr,

00:02:31.117 --> 00:02:33.219
Democratic senator of Connecticut,

00:02:33.219 --> 00:02:34.621
where obviously Durham

00:02:34.621 --> 00:02:36.156
Practice and practices,

00:02:36.156 --> 00:02:37.390
Chris Murphy told CNN

00:02:37.390 --> 00:02:38.791
he had a, quote, reputation

00:02:38.791 --> 00:02:41.060
of being apolitical and serious.

00:02:41.427 --> 00:02:44.130
So among the things that he concluded is

00:02:44.164 --> 00:02:46.299
he says the FBI under your purview

00:02:46.299 --> 00:02:47.300
in this investigation

00:02:47.300 --> 00:02:48.001
displayed a, quote,

00:02:48.001 --> 00:02:50.036
lack of analytical rigor. That's a quote.

00:02:50.270 --> 00:02:52.305
He also said that you used, quote, raw

00:02:52.305 --> 00:02:52.939
un analyze

00:02:52.939 --> 00:02:54.541
an uncooperative intelligence

00:02:54.541 --> 00:02:55.542
to launch investigation

00:02:55.542 --> 00:02:57.877
and makes the accusation that essentially

00:02:58.311 --> 00:03:00.413
you guys use different standards

00:03:00.413 --> 00:03:02.882
for which to launch this

00:03:02.882 --> 00:03:05.218
as opposed to probe into Hillary Clinton.

00:03:05.251 --> 00:03:07.320
What's your response?

00:03:07.654 --> 00:03:09.889
Yeah, that's that's entirely inaccurate.

00:03:10.456 --> 00:03:12.358
He's got a lot packed into that question.

00:03:12.358 --> 00:03:13.993
So I'll address a couple of those points,

00:03:13.993 --> 00:03:15.595
if that's okay.

00:03:15.595 --> 00:03:17.597
The investigation was initiated

00:03:17.730 --> 00:03:19.098
not based on raw,

00:03:19.098 --> 00:03:20.967
uncorroborated intelligence,

00:03:20.967 --> 00:03:24.103
but but on significant understanding

00:03:24.103 --> 00:03:26.105
and awareness of what the Russians

00:03:26.105 --> 00:03:26.973
were doing.

00:03:26.973 --> 00:03:27.941
In their

00:03:28.007 --> 00:03:29.342
multipronged effort

00:03:29.342 --> 00:03:31.344
to influence the 2016 election.

00:03:31.377 --> 00:03:31.945
We knew

00:03:31.945 --> 00:03:32.445
the Russians

00:03:32.445 --> 00:03:34.380
had been targeting us in cyberspace.

00:03:34.380 --> 00:03:36.416
We knew the Russians had been going after

00:03:36.416 --> 00:03:37.917
and stealing

00:03:37.951 --> 00:03:39.152
electronic information

00:03:39.152 --> 00:03:41.087
from our political institutions,

00:03:41.087 --> 00:03:42.422
from government institutions

00:03:42.422 --> 00:03:44.190
for over a year

00:03:44.190 --> 00:03:46.993
until the beginning of of 2016

00:03:46.993 --> 00:03:47.827
we knew they targeted

00:03:47.827 --> 00:03:50.296
the DNC and exfiltrated

00:03:50.296 --> 00:03:51.764
an enormous amount of information

00:03:51.764 --> 00:03:52.932
about Hillary Clinton.

00:03:52.932 --> 00:03:54.167
And then we knew that

00:03:54.167 --> 00:03:56.502
the Russian Russians use that information

00:03:56.703 --> 00:03:58.638
in an effort to impact the election

00:03:58.638 --> 00:03:59.872
by releasing

00:03:59.872 --> 00:04:00.673
those emails

00:04:00.673 --> 00:04:02.041
on the eve of the Democratic

00:04:02.041 --> 00:04:03.276
National Convention.

00:04:03.276 --> 00:04:05.011
We only found out later

00:04:05.011 --> 00:04:06.512
at the end of July

00:04:06.512 --> 00:04:07.480
that prior

00:04:07.480 --> 00:04:09.215
to weaponizing that information,

00:04:09.215 --> 00:04:11.317
they'd made essentially an offer

00:04:11.317 --> 00:04:12.785
to the Trump campaign

00:04:12.785 --> 00:04:13.987
that they had information

00:04:13.987 --> 00:04:15.154
about Hillary Clinton

00:04:15.154 --> 00:04:16.889
and that they would use it

00:04:16.889 --> 00:04:18.391
to benefit the Trump campaign.

00:04:18.391 --> 00:04:20.193
So with that understanding

00:04:20.193 --> 00:04:22.262
of what the Russians were doing,

00:04:22.462 --> 00:04:24.063
we had the question

00:04:24.063 --> 00:04:24.998
the very real

00:04:24.998 --> 00:04:26.132
and very significant question

00:04:26.132 --> 00:04:26.833
of whether

00:04:26.833 --> 00:04:28.968
or not members of a domestic

00:04:28.968 --> 00:04:30.069
political campaign

00:04:30.069 --> 00:04:31.537
had conspired with

00:04:31.537 --> 00:04:33.473
or taken assistance from the Russians.

00:04:33.473 --> 00:04:34.841
We didn't know if they had

00:04:34.841 --> 00:04:36.876
we didn't know who that might have been,

00:04:36.876 --> 00:04:38.244
but we knew that it was something

00:04:38.244 --> 00:04:40.013
that had to be investigated.

00:04:40.013 --> 00:04:41.981
That's the opening of the case

00:04:41.981 --> 00:04:43.616
that, as I said, the IG

00:04:43.616 --> 00:04:45.718
and other investigative entities

00:04:45.718 --> 00:04:48.421
approved of that action in hindsight.

00:04:48.554 --> 00:04:49.589
And he also included

00:04:49.589 --> 00:04:50.523
in Durham's report

00:04:50.523 --> 00:04:52.091
are disparaging text messages

00:04:52.091 --> 00:04:53.526
about former President Trump.

00:04:53.526 --> 00:04:54.594
I'll just highlight this one.

00:04:54.594 --> 00:04:55.495
We can show our viewers.

00:04:55.495 --> 00:04:55.895
This is on

00:04:55.895 --> 00:04:58.264
August 15th, 2016, about two weeks

00:04:58.264 --> 00:04:59.899
after the investigation was launched

00:04:59.899 --> 00:05:01.200
between two key

00:05:01.200 --> 00:05:03.736
team members, Peter Strzok and Lisa Page.

00:05:03.736 --> 00:05:04.470
Here it is, quote,

00:05:04.470 --> 00:05:05.705
I want to believe the past

00:05:05.705 --> 00:05:06.272
you threw out

00:05:06.272 --> 00:05:08.341
for consideration in Andy's office

00:05:08.474 --> 00:05:09.742
that there is no way he,

00:05:09.742 --> 00:05:11.110
meaning Trump, gets elected.

00:05:11.110 --> 00:05:12.879
But I'm afraid we can't take that risk.

00:05:12.879 --> 00:05:14.147
It's like an insurance policy

00:05:14.147 --> 00:05:15.581
in the unlikely event that you die

00:05:15.581 --> 00:05:17.250
before you're 40.

00:05:17.250 --> 00:05:17.950
That obviously

00:05:17.950 --> 00:05:19.018
has gotten a lot of attention

00:05:19.018 --> 00:05:19.952
for many years.

00:05:19.952 --> 00:05:20.787
You said last night

00:05:20.787 --> 00:05:21.387
to my colleague

00:05:21.387 --> 00:05:22.488
Anderson Cooper, look, that

00:05:22.488 --> 00:05:23.956
was, quote, objectionable

00:05:23.956 --> 00:05:25.425
and unfortunate.

00:05:25.425 --> 00:05:26.426
Is there a lesson learned

00:05:26.426 --> 00:05:28.528
for the agency writ large

00:05:28.528 --> 00:05:30.229
from exchanges like that?

00:05:31.564 --> 00:05:31.998
I think there's

00:05:31.998 --> 00:05:32.765
a lot of lessons

00:05:32.765 --> 00:05:33.866
learned for the agency

00:05:33.866 --> 00:05:35.134
and certainly for those two

00:05:35.134 --> 00:05:35.802
individual aides

00:05:35.802 --> 00:05:35.935
who were

00:05:35.935 --> 00:05:38.671
involved in in those communications.

00:05:39.706 --> 00:05:40.907
If you're asking me,

00:05:40.907 --> 00:05:42.742
did the agency learn that they should now

00:05:42.742 --> 00:05:44.410
monitor the private communications

00:05:44.410 --> 00:05:45.511
of all their employees

00:05:45.511 --> 00:05:46.245
to safeguard

00:05:46.245 --> 00:05:49.515
against the occurrences like this?

00:05:49.549 --> 00:05:52.051
No, I don't believe that's true.

00:05:52.051 --> 00:05:55.488
But there's no place in the FBI

00:05:55.755 --> 00:05:58.524
for people involved in an investigation

00:05:58.524 --> 00:05:59.792
to be approaching that work

00:05:59.792 --> 00:06:01.928
from a politically motivated standpoint.

00:06:01.928 --> 00:06:03.129
And I can tell you right now

00:06:03.129 --> 00:06:04.163
that at no time

00:06:04.163 --> 00:06:06.199
did I or anyone to my knowledge

00:06:06.199 --> 00:06:08.267
understand that Peter Strzok

00:06:08.267 --> 00:06:10.570
or Lisa Page harbored those.

00:06:10.837 --> 00:06:11.304
We're having

00:06:11.304 --> 00:06:13.272
those sorts of conversations.

00:06:13.272 --> 00:06:14.741
Neither of the two of them

00:06:14.741 --> 00:06:15.641
ever gave me

00:06:15.641 --> 00:06:17.210
or anyone else that I'm aware of.

00:06:17.210 --> 00:06:18.144
Any indication

00:06:18.144 --> 00:06:20.913
that their work on this investigation

00:06:21.114 --> 00:06:23.282
was being influenced by the professional,

00:06:23.282 --> 00:06:25.685
by their personal opinions

00:06:25.685 --> 00:06:28.321
So and that that stands to this day.

00:06:28.755 --> 00:06:30.823
And just to put a button on it,

00:06:31.057 --> 00:06:32.492
because of the point you made up in terms

00:06:32.492 --> 00:06:34.160
of not letting anything in terms

00:06:34.160 --> 00:06:35.461
of personal political beliefs

00:06:35.461 --> 00:06:36.829
interfere with the work that is done.

00:06:36.829 --> 00:06:38.131
I thought it was interesting

00:06:38.131 --> 00:06:39.699
that in this report, Durham

00:06:39.699 --> 00:06:42.869
suggested creating a sort of a position

00:06:42.869 --> 00:06:44.637
for a nonpartisan FBI

00:06:44.637 --> 00:06:45.705
lawyer or agent

00:06:45.705 --> 00:06:50.543
who would essentially step in and oversee

00:06:50.543 --> 00:06:50.977
and help

00:06:50.977 --> 00:06:52.311
put checks on anything

00:06:52.311 --> 00:06:53.012
that would be deemed

00:06:53.012 --> 00:06:55.114
a politically sensitive investigation.

00:06:55.381 --> 00:06:56.616
Do you think that's a good idea?

00:06:59.385 --> 00:07:00.920
It's not a bad idea,

00:07:00.920 --> 00:07:02.622
but I don't think it's necessary.

00:07:02.622 --> 00:07:03.356
I mean, look,

00:07:03.356 --> 00:07:04.290
that person

00:07:04.290 --> 00:07:06.959
that's that role, that voice exists

00:07:06.959 --> 00:07:09.028
in the FBI to this today.

00:07:09.228 --> 00:07:11.764
And that's the general counsel of the FBI

00:07:11.931 --> 00:07:12.765
and the staff

00:07:12.765 --> 00:07:14.600
of the general counsel's office,

00:07:14.600 --> 00:07:16.669
including dozens of attorneys

00:07:16.836 --> 00:07:19.338
who do nothing but advise the FBI

00:07:19.539 --> 00:07:20.440
on the implications

00:07:20.440 --> 00:07:22.175
of their national security work.

00:07:22.175 --> 00:07:23.676
Those people, Jim Baker,

00:07:23.676 --> 00:07:25.011
who is who is general counsel

00:07:25.011 --> 00:07:25.745
at the time,

00:07:25.745 --> 00:07:27.814
and many of the lawyers who work for him

00:07:27.814 --> 00:07:30.450
were present in all of the meetings

00:07:30.450 --> 00:07:31.217
in which

00:07:31.217 --> 00:07:32.752
opening this investigation

00:07:32.752 --> 00:07:34.220
and conducting this investigative

00:07:34.220 --> 00:07:35.521
matter were discussed.

00:07:35.521 --> 00:07:37.523
And we had those conversations

00:07:37.523 --> 00:07:39.459
about what the implications would be,

00:07:39.459 --> 00:07:41.160
the legality of what we were doing,

00:07:41.160 --> 00:07:43.029
the authority behind the steps

00:07:43.029 --> 00:07:43.796
that we were taking.

00:07:43.796 --> 00:07:46.432
So those conversations happened.

00:07:46.732 --> 00:07:47.400
If Mr.

00:07:47.400 --> 00:07:48.901
Durham and then

00:07:48.901 --> 00:07:49.602
in a failure

00:07:49.602 --> 00:07:50.203
to come up with

00:07:50.203 --> 00:07:53.339
any other significant recommendations, is

00:07:53.372 --> 00:07:54.040
suggesting that

00:07:54.040 --> 00:07:55.541
the FBI should have another lawyer,

00:07:55.541 --> 00:07:56.342
I think that's great.

00:07:56.342 --> 00:07:57.443
They should have another lawyer.

00:07:57.443 --> 00:07:59.612
I'm sure they have plenty of work to do.

00:07:59.612 --> 00:08:01.080
But those kind of conversations,

00:08:01.080 --> 00:08:02.215
that sort of oversight

00:08:02.215 --> 00:08:03.282
that he's suggesting

00:08:03.282 --> 00:08:04.484
is already taking place

00:08:04.484 --> 00:08:06.385
and has always taken place in the FBI.

00:08:06.385 --> 00:08:08.054
Andrew McCabe, thank you very, very much.

00:08:08.054 --> 00:08:09.155
Obviously, you were critical

00:08:09.155 --> 00:08:10.056
in this investigation.

00:08:10.056 --> 00:08:11.324
Appreciate you answering questions

00:08:11.324 --> 00:08:11.824
this morning.

